Carafe Lab: under NCE a 39-bit process keeps its whole 512 GiB address space, as on the console. Eden cut it to
256 GiB and reserved as much host space for phones with a 39-bit host address space; the lab's host has 48 bits.
Autorun refuses to start an AMD64 program when the address space ends below 512 GiB ("AMD64 requires the 39-bit
forwarder"), so every 64-bit game stopped before its first frame. Under NCE the guest's addresses are the host's,
and Eden maps guest memory only inside its host reservation, which sat at a random place from 64 GiB up: guest
pages below it were never mapped. The reservation now starts at 128 MiB, where the guest's address space starts,
and covers all of it; a random place is tried as before when that range is taken.
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the files it changes.

--- a/src/common/host_memory.cpp
+++ b/src/common/host_memory.cpp
@@ -404,6 +404,19 @@ static void* ChooseVirtualBase(size_t virtual_size) {
 
     // We want to ensure we are allocating at an address aligned to the L2 block size.
     // For Qualcomm devices, we must also allocate memory above 36 bits.
+    constexpr uintptr_t GuestSpaceStart = 128ULL << 20;
+    void* guest_window = mmap(reinterpret_cast<void*>(GuestSpaceStart), virtual_size, PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE,
+                              MAP_PRIVATE | MAP_ANONYMOUS | MAP_NORESERVE | MAP_FIXED_NOREPLACE, -1, 0);
+    if (reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(guest_window) == GuestSpaceStart) {
+        return guest_window;
+    }
+    if (guest_window != MAP_FAILED) {
+        munmap(guest_window, virtual_size);
+    }
+    if (virtual_size >= Map39BitSize - Map36BitSize) {
+        return MAP_FAILED;
+    }
+
     const size_t lower = Map36BitSize / HugePageSize;
     const size_t upper = (Map39BitSize - virtual_size) / HugePageSize;
     const size_t range = upper - lower;
